.TH SDE-AUTOSTART 1 "October 2026" "SDE 0.1 Alpha" "Selviana Desktop Environment"
.SH NAME
sde-autostart \- Rust XDG autostart launcher for SDE
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sde-autostart
[\-\-dry-run | \-\-version | \-\-help]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Normally called once by sde-session. Reads desktop entries from
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart and $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/autostart. The first file with
each name takes precedence, including a user file with Hidden=true.
Honors OnlyShowIn, NotShowIn, TryExec, Terminal and Path. NoDisplay does not
disable autostart. Exec is expanded into an argument vector without a shell.
Polkit agents and notification daemons managed by SDE are skipped.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Print the launch plan and skip reasons without starting any applications.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the SDE version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means the plan or launch requests succeeded; it does not mean applications
remained running. 1 means a directory, entry or launch failed; other entries
are still processed when an individual entry fails. 2 means invalid arguments.
.SH NOTES
No autostart delays, desktop-specific condition expressions or D-Bus-only
activation are implemented. Do not call the launcher twice in one session.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sde-session (1)
